    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Early evacuation of large lobar hematomas may be lifesaving, but rebleeding occurs frequently; early evacuation of deep hematomas is seldom indicated (surgical mortality is high and deficits are usually severe)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "With hydrocephalus (a predictor of worse outcome), surgeons may place an external ventricular drain to rapidly lower ICP; this can be lifesaving"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Antiseizure medications are used only if the patient has had a seizure, not typically prophylactically"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
